# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Full abstract text pulled from NCBI. Deliberately not committed: the repo
# ships derived data (PMIDs, citation metadata, extracted spans, short
# excerpts) rather than redistributing publisher-copyrighted abstracts.
# Rebuild with `python scripts/build_literature_snapshot.py`.
.cache/
# An older build script wrote full text here instead of .cache/. Kept as a
# guard: a stray abstracts/ is 76 publisher abstracts one `git add -A` away
# from being redistributed, which is the one line this repo doesn't cross.
/abstracts/

# Generated by the dashboard build. `docs/dashboard.png` is the committed
# screenshot the README embeds; these two are rebuilt per run.
src/target_intel/dashboard/dashboard.html
src/target_intel/dashboard/portfolio_report.json

# Regenerated by `target-intel eval`
evals/eval_report.json

# Application material, not project material. These are the candidate-facing
# documents that go with the submission email and the Loom - a public repo
# full of "why hire me" undercuts the work it's arguing for.
/APPLICATION_NOTE.md
/HANDOFF.md
/LOOM_SCRIPT.md
/COMMIT_PLAN.md
/dashboard_preview.png

# Secrets
.env
